  "goodToKnow": "Das Welterbe is World Heritage, UNESCO's list of outstanding sites: Weltkulturerbe (cultural) and Weltnaturerbe (natural). Germany has more than 50 sites, including Cologne Cathedral, the Wadden Sea, Bauhaus buildings and the Upper Middle Rhine Valley. The Dresden Elbe Valley lost its status in 2009 after the city built the Waldschlößchenbrücke. Das Erbe means inheritance or heritage. It has no plural."
